  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mo>⊕</mo></math> and <math><mo>⊗</mo></math> are two mathematical operators. If <math><mi>p</mi><mo>⊕</mo></math> <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⊗</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is not a tautology, then <math><mo>⊕</mo></math> and <math><mo>⊗</mo></math> can be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8744;</mo></math> and <math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> respectively",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mo>⇒</mo></math> and <math><mo>∧</mo></math> respectively",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> and <math><mo>∨</mo></math> respectively",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "None of these",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math><mi>p</mi><mo>∨</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is false only if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> is false and&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is false which is never possible simultaneously. Hence,&nbsp;<math><mi>p</mi><mo>∨</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a tautology<br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math><mi>p</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is false only if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> is true and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is false which is never possible simultaneously. Hence,&nbsp;<math><mi>p</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a tautology<br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math><mi>p</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is false only if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> is true &amp; <math><mi>p</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>q</mi></math> is false which is possible when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> is true &amp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> is false. Hence,&nbsp;<math><mi>p</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is not a tautology"
  }
}